<p><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" src="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-23-long-distance.png" alt="de moraes chess puzzle" width="383" height="387" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-73813" srcset="https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-23-long-distance.png 383w, https://www.futilitycloset.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-07-23-long-distance-300x303.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 383px) 100vw, 383px" /></p>
<p>In this classic puzzle by Florencio Mendes de Moraes, White must checkmate Black in seven moves. The catch is that all three of his queens are confined to the leftmost file.</p>
<p>Either of two first moves will get things started, but beyond that there&#8217;s only one sequence that will work. What is it?</p>

